    "summary": "Man’s gown (boubou, tobe, riga) made from four sheets of European cream coloured cotton sheeting, assembled into a rectangular gown with square body and flared sleeves. At the front is a vestigial large pocket made from another sheet of cotton and sewn down. The area around the neck opening at the front is hand-embroidered in European green cotton with a small pattern of ‘two knives’ (aska biyu) and a spiral; another spiral is on the back of the neck. The sleeves and base of the garment are hemmed using a sewing machine.",
